                  "avatarUrls" : {
                     "16x16" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "24x24" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "32x32" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
                  },
                  "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
                  "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
                  "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
               },
               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "This makes a ton of sense. Not clear how to accomodate this in teh current API, however. MAYBE differnt subclasses of SortedMultiSet (sortedByCountMultiSet). Maybe optional parameter to SortedMultiSet constructor - a sort-function that operates on teh value.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Internally, could use multimap<count,T> to achieve this, maybe. Not a great data structure. Could maintain two data structures - existing map<> and a separate map<count,T>? Like bijection does.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Or just maintain an unordered list (or array) and sort as needed for particular purposes? NOT really sure best how todo this.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "attrs" : {
                                 "id" : "557058:00982330-393c-42b6-b6fe-9cb70700fd96",
                                 "text" : "@Sterling Wight"
                              },
                              "type" : "mention"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : " alot depends on how BIG and performance sorts of issues. Do you care not a whit for the order of items that all share a count?",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Maybe should have a method of Tally called something like GetTop() - that returns the top N items (by count). Maybe dont use sorted tally at all. Maybe this is the wrong suggestion.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "MAYBE all you REALLY want is a getTopN() that gets you a list of items sorted by count, and maybe have an IMPLEMENTATION that makes this efficient?",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
                  ],
                  "type" : "doc",
                  "version" : 1
               },
