               },
               "updated" : "2022-11-10T17:05:20.645-0500"
            },
            {
               "author" : {
                  "accountId" : "557058:4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
                  "accountType" : "atlassian",
                  "active" : true,
                  "avatarUrls" : {
                     "16x16" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "24x24" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "32x32" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
                     "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
                  },
                  "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
                  "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
                  "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
               },
               "body" : {
                  "content" : [
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Thought more about this. As a data structure problem, this probably does NOT make sense. NEEDED to keep map KEY->count info, to support adds. That CANNOT map backwards (without lots of extra gorp). Easist way would be to keep two data structures - mapping in both directions (like bijection). But that would be a lot of cost. Worth while if no better way, but there is a better way for most use cases.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "New API ",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "content" : [
                                 {
                                    "text" : "Iterable<T>::Top()",
                                    "type" : "text"
                                 }
                              ],
                              "type" : "paragraph"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "blockquote"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "Takes function param (sort order). And optional max count. Then very efficeintly (OR N * LOG(fix num returned count) ) - so effectively for Top(3) - O(N).",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "This can then be shaddowned in the Mutliset class.",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "type" : "hardBreak"
                           },
                           {
                              "text" : "So if you want items -in count order just say:",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "content" : [
                                 {
                                    "text" : "Multiset<int> x;",
                                    "type" : "text"
                                 }
                              ],
                              "type" : "paragraph"
                           },
                           {
                              "content" : [
                                 {
                                    "text" : "x.Top (3) - and you get a list of the top three items.",
                                    "type" : "text"
                                 }
                              ],
                              "type" : "paragraph"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "blockquote"
                     },
                     {
                        "content" : [
                           {
                              "text" : "For case where you BUILD list and then call Top () once, this is STRICTLY more efficient than any other data structure I know of to produce this answer. ONYL benefit of keeping data in Multiset object is if calling repeatedly to get Top (N).",
                              "type" : "text"
                           }
                        ],
                        "type" : "paragraph"
                     }
                  ],
                  "type" : "doc",
                  "version" : 1
               },
